Subject: Fit the playlist footer: a bare count for an empty playlist, a zero position formatted, a shortest form for a narrow column

The playlist footer took the "%1 tracks, %2 total" branch for an empty
playlist, whose remainingTracks is -1, and ProgressIndicator left its
text empty at position 0: it formats only in setPosition(), which
returns early when the position is unchanged and the position starts at
0. The footer reads "0 tracks,  total". Give an empty playlist its own
branch, which reads "0 tracks" through the existing "%1 track" string.
Format the starting position in the constructor, through the same
helper setPosition() uses, so every ProgressIndicator bound to 0 reads
"00:00": the duration slider's labels before anything has played, and a
playlist whose tracks have no known length.

The footer picks the longest of three forms that fits the label, but
the shortest, "1/2 tracks, 00:06/00:07 remaining", is wider than the
playlist column at the window's default size, so it is elided
mid-word. Add a fourth form without the remaining time, "1/2 tracks,
00:07 total", for a column too narrow for the third, and measure every
form in the label's own font rather than its family alone, so a form is
chosen only when it fits as drawn.

